# Deck generation retention (next steps)

When working on schema-driven deck gen / Phase B, remember these follow-ons (also in `local/schema-driven-deck-generation-engine/NEXT-STEPS.md`):

- **Review packages** (`draft.pptx` + truth/exemplar PNGs + `manifest.json`) are Cursor scratch space → S3 with a **short lifecycle** (e.g. 7–30 days). Do not treat them as the long-term archive.
- **Associate / audit access** needs the **final PPTX** (optional light metadata), not the full PNG review tree.
- **SharePoint** is the preferred place for finished decks humans need (permissions, search, retention). Do not dump full review packages into SharePoint by default.
- **S3 lifecycle ≠ token savings.** Vision token cost is controlled by how many PNGs Cursor sees and how many loops run (B3), not by storage location.
